{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgucBfQhzpM21kQPLiRhj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the route to `route.camel.yaml`. I haven't run or validated it in Camel.\n\n```yaml\n- route:\n    id: nightly-order-export\n    from:\n      uri: quartz:orderExport/nightly\n      parameters:\n        cron: \"0 0 2 * * ?\"\n        trigger.timeZone: Europe/Berlin\n      steps:\n        - log:\n            message: Nightly order export started\n        - to:\n            uri: direct:export\n```\n\n- **Trigger:** `quartz:orderExport/nightly` is a Quartz timer named `nightly` in the group `orderExport`.\n- **Schedule:** `cron: \"0 0 2 * * ?\"` fires at 02:00:00 every day. Quartz cron has six fields: seconds, minutes, hours, day-of-month, month, day-of-week. One of the two day fields has to be `?`.\n- **Time zone:** `trigger.timeZone: Europe/Berlin` makes the cron run on Berlin time, including the switch between summer and winter time. Without it, it would use the JVM's default time zone.\n- **Steps:** the route logs \"Nightly order export started\" and then sends the message to `direct:export`.\n\nYour Camel project needs the `camel-quartz` dependency for this to run."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":703,"cache_read_input_tokens":4517,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":703},"output_tokens":421,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3e1d3e2-e3f7-4866-a273-63153f1beaaa","uuid":"6109878d-4521-47a7-95d5-bffb390c39bc","timestamp":"2026-11-10T17:02:15.182Z","request_id":"req_011CgucBfEnN1G5N3ReAhYSB"}
